    <h3>Now: being built</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Sold-out items and "5 left" counts, straight from the register</li>
      <li>Two devices working on one check at once</li>
      <li>Floor and table views on every device</li>
      <li>A register layout that fits your screen, including short laptop screens</li>
      <li>Paid and unpaid breaks on the time clock</li>
      <li>Kitchen: one item sent to two stations, ticket options, coursing, and recovery when a printer stops mid-service</li>
      <li>A bump bar and number pad for the kitchen screen</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Next: planned</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>A Reports section beside the Dashboard</li>
      <li>Named discounts staff can tap</li>
      <li>Notes and labels on a check that reach the kitchen</li>
      <li>Bar, dining room and patio as separate areas, each with its own floor plan and reports</li>
      <li>Moving items and checks between tables</li>
      <li>Reasons recorded on voids, cancels and discounts</li>
      <li>Connections to accounting tools and to delivery orders</li>
      <li>Finer permissions for each setup screen</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>Later: ideas</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Menus and prices that change by time of day</li>
      <li>Tax-exempt checks and open-priced items</li>
      <li>Receipt templates</li>
      <li>Easier setup: staff import and a go-live checklist</li>
      <li>Labor rules</li>
